{
  "abstract": "A formalization of a proof of Swanepoel's Conjecture on Penny Graphs. The conjecture asks for the maximum number of edges in a triangle-free penny graph on n vertices. Let this quantity be denoted as f(n). Previous results have shown that f(n) >= floor(2n - 2 square root n). Prior work proved the approximate upper bound f(n) <= floor(2n - 1.65 square root of n). This work formalizes a proof that the upper bound is the conjectured floor(2n - 2 square root of n). This result proves the stated conjecture unconditionally and affirmatively.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Naveen Stewart"
    }
  ],
